@node Capture
@section Capture

@findex slack-extras-personal-capture
The command @code{slack-extras-personal-capture} captures the Slack message at point to the personal inbox via @code{org-capture} template @samp{s}. It is bound to @samp{o} in @code{slack-activity-feed-buffer-mode-map}, @code{slack-thread-message-buffer-mode-map} and @code{slack-message-buffer-mode-map}.

@findex slack-extras-work-capture
The command @code{slack-extras-work-capture} captures the Slack message at point to the work inbox via @code{org-capture} template @samp{S}. It is bound to @samp{E} in @code{slack-activity-feed-buffer-mode-map}, @code{slack-thread-message-buffer-mode-map} and @code{slack-message-buffer-mode-map}.

@node ActivityWatch context
@chapter ActivityWatch context

@findex slack-extras-activity-watch-data
When @samp{activity-watch-mode} is loaded, @code{slack-extras-activity-watch-data} contributes channel and workspace names and IDs through @code{activity-watch-data-functions}. It reads the room object already held by the sampled Slack buffer. This lets a time tracker use the selected channel rather than the buffer's unrelated inherited working directory.

Public and private channels, including their threads, provide channel context. Direct messages, group direct messages and mixed-room views provide only workspace context, allowing work conversations to remain general work without inventing a project. The integration reads no messages and makes no network requests. ActivityWatch receives the metadata only when its watcher samples the selected buffer of a focused frame.

@node Tab-bar notifications
@chapter Tab-bar notifications

@vindex tab-bar-extras-slack-notifications-enabled
The variable @code{tab-bar-extras-slack-notifications-enabled} controls whether the Slack notification element is displayed in the tab bar. It defaults to @code{t}.

@findex slack-extras-actionable-unreads-p
The function @code{slack-extras-actionable-unreads-p} determines whether there are Slack notifications worth the user's attention. It triggers a debounced refresh of the Activity feed unread summary and returns the value of @code{slack-has-unreads}.

The tab-bar element @code{tab-bar-extras-slack-element} displays a Slack icon (from @samp{nerd-icons}) and a badge when @code{slack-extras-actionable-unreads-p} returns non-nil. The badge shows the total mention count, or a bullet (@code{•}) when there are actionable unreads but no @@mentions (such as thread replies or DMs). Registration appends the element to @code{tab-bar-extras-global-mode-string} and immediately syncs @code{global-mode-string} via @code{tab-bar-extras-set-global-mode-string}, so the badge appears even when @samp{slack-extras} loads after the initial tab-bar sync.

@findex tab-bar-extras-toggle-slack-notifications
The command @code{tab-bar-extras-toggle-slack-notifications} toggles Slack notifications in the tab bar. It also participates in the master toggle: when @code{tab-bar-extras-toggle-notifications} is called, Slack notifications are toggled along with the other notification sources.

